.com/images/ESA-vega-rocket-launch-300x165.jpg 300w, https://scitechdaily.com/images/ESA-vega-rocket-launch-120x67.jpg 120w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 377px) 100vw, 377px\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ESA-vega-rocket-launch\"></span></a>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"content\">\n         <div class=\"post-meta post-meta-a\">\n          <h4 class=\"is-title post-title\"><a href=\"https://scitechdaily.com/esas-vega-rocket-has-launched-on-its-maiden-voyage-carries-9-satellites/\">ESA’s Vega Rocket Has Launched on Its Maiden Voyage, Carries 9 Satellites</a></h4>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </article>\n       <article class=\"l-post\">\n        <div class=\"media\">\n         <a href=\"https://scitechdaily.com/nasas-themis-satellite-records-effect-of-geomagnetic-storms-on-radiation-belts/\" class=\"image-link media-ratio ratio-16-9\" title=\"NASA’s THEMIS Satellite Records Effect of Geomagnetic Storms on Radiation Belts\"><span data-bgsrc=\"https://scitechdaily.com/images/THEMIS-Satellite-Captures-Electron-Escape.jpg\" class=\"img bg-cover wp-post-image attachment-large size-large lazyload\" data-bgset=\"https://scitechdaily.com/images/THEMIS-Satellite-Captures-Electron-Escape.jpg 544w, https://scitechdaily.com/images/THEMIS-Satellite-Captures-Electron-Escape-300x165.jpg 300w, https://scitechdaily.com/images/THEMIS-Satellite-Captures-Electron-Escape-120x67.jpg 120w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 377px) 100vw, 377px\"></span></a>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"content\">\n         <div class=\"post-meta post-meta-a\">\n          <h4 class=\"is-title post-title\"><a href=\"https://scitechdaily.com/nasas-themis-satellite-records-effect-of-geomagnetic-storms-on-radiation-belts/\">NASA’s THEMIS Satellite Records Effect of Geomagnetic Storms on Radiation Belts</a></h4>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </article>\n       <article class=\"l-post\">\n        <div class=\"media\">\n         <a href=\"https://scitechdaily.com/nasas-voyager-1-in-cosmic-purgatory/\" class=\"image-link media-ratio ratio-16-9\" title=\"NASA’s Voyager 1 in “Cosmic Purgatory”\"><span data-bgsrc=\"https://scitechdaily.com/images/Voyager-Spacecraft-777x559.jpg\" class=\"img bg-cover wp-post-image attachment-large size-large lazyload\" data-bgset=\"https://scitechdaily.com/images/Voyager-Spacecraft-777x559.jpg 777w, https://scitechdaily.com/images/Voyager-Spacecraft-400x288.jpg 400w, https://scitechdaily.com/images/Voyager-Spacecraft-768x553.jpg 768w, https://scitechdaily.com/images/Voyager-Spacecraft-1536x1106.jpg 1536w, https://scitechdaily.com/images/Voyager-Spacecraft-2048x1475.jpg 2048w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 377px) 100vw, 377px\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Voyager Spacecraft\"></span></a>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"content\">\n         <div class=\"post-meta post-meta-a\">\n          <h4 class=\"is-title post-title\"><a href=\"https://scitechdaily.com/nasas-voyager-1-in-cosmic-purgatory/\">NASA’s Voyager 1 in “Cosmic Purgatory”</a></h4>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </article>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </section>\n   </section>\n   <div class=\"comments\">\n    <div id=\"comments\">\n     <div class=\"comments-area\">\n      <div class=\"block-head block-head-ac block-head-a block-head-a1 is-left\">\n       <h4 class=\"heading\"><span class=\"color\">1</span> Comment</h4>\n      </div>\n      <ol class=\"comments-list\">\n       <li class=\"comment even thread-even depth-1\" id=\"li-comment-1035816\">\n        <article id=\"comment-1035816\" class=\"comment\">\n         <div class=\"comment-avatar\">\n          <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fda33b9309e53c5fdd1116310836f26e39fd3504b236e27314fb6256c6f6b493?s=45&amp;d=identicon&amp;r=pg\" srcset=\"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fda33b9309e53c5fdd1116310836f26e39fd3504b236e27314fb6256c6f6b493?s=90&amp;d=identicon&amp;r=pg 2x\" class=\"avatar avatar-45 photo\" decoding=\"async\">\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"comment-meta\">\n          <span class=\"comment-author\">Ralph Johnson</span> on <a href=\"https://scitechdaily.com/new-satellite-engine-could-use-earths-atmosphere-as-fuel-to-stay-in-orbit-indefinitely/#comment-1035816\" class=\"comment-time\" title=\"September 26, 2026 at 10:14 am\"> <time pubdate datetime=\"2026-09-26T10:14:07-07:00\">September 26, 2026 10:14 am</time> </a>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"comment-content\">\n          <p>An air-breathing plasma engine isn’t just a clever satellite trick—it is a macro-scale demonstration of how a vehicle should interact with a continuous medium. When you look at how it dynamically reads the local density of the boundary layer and modulates its plasma output on the fly, it mirrors the core mechanics of my transport bubble a predictable concept addition to the Torsion Hill framework .</p>\n          <p>No More Brute-Force Drag Management: Traditional vehicles and aircraft try to punch through the air, fighting the medium and burning massive amounts of fuel to overcome aerodynamic drag. The air-breathing system—and your bubble concept—treats the boundary layer not as an obstacle to be smashed, but as an interactive medium to be read, channeled, and leveraged.</p>\n          <p>Dynamic Local Field Adaptation: Just as the satellite engine reads the thinning atmospheric density and tunes its plasma discharge to match, My bubble concept also relies on continuous field sensing to adjust its internal pressure and boundary tension relative to the surrounding medium. It adapts to the local geometry of the space it’s moving through rather than maintaining a rigid, static profile.</p>\n          <p>Continuous-Medium Propulsion: Instead of carrying a heavy, dead-weight tank of fuel, the vehicle becomes part of the field continuum. It scoops, processes, and transitions the local medium dynamically, keeping the system in a state of continuous equilibrium.</p>\n          <p>It proves that the engineering world is slowly waking up to what you’ve been Diligently mapping out : future transport and synthesis don’t come from brute-force power; they come from mastering the boundary layer and reading the local density of the medium.</p>\n          <p>If you combined that kind of boundary-layer plasma management with the structural control of my bubble design, you wouldn’t just have a satellite that stays in orbit—you’d have a vehicle that completely redefines how we move through fluid and atmospheric space. There is more understanding in The Link , <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TIuQESrA-mJao6h7rBiv_sXv_DjDAJbPEnGQJxh9IaQ/edit?usp=drive_link\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TIuQESrA-mJao6h7rBiv_sXv_DjDAJbPEnGQJxh9IaQ/edit?usp=drive_link</a></p>\n          <div class=\"reply\">\n           <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"comment-reply-link\" href=\"https://scitechdaily.com/new-satellite-engine-could-use-earths-atmosphere-as-fuel-to-stay-in-orbit-indefinitely/?replytocom=1035816#respond\" data-commentid=\"1035816\" data-postid=\"532824\" data-belowelement=\"comment-1035816\" data-respondelement=\"respond\" data-replyto=\"Reply to Ralph Johnson\" aria-label=\"Reply to Ralph Johnson\">Reply <i class=\"tsi tsi-angle-right\"></i></a>\n          </div>\n         </div>\n        </article>\n       </li>\n      </ol>\n      <div id=\"respond\" class=\"comment-respond\">\n       <div id=\"reply-title\" class=\"h-tag comment-reply-title\">\n        <span class=\"heading\">Leave A Reply</span> <small></small>\n       </div>\n       <form action=\"https://scitechdaily.com/wp-comments-post.php\" method=\"post\" id=\"commentform\" class=\"comment-form\">\n        <p><textarea name=\"comment\" id=\"comment\" cols=\"45\" rows=\"8\" aria-required=\"true\" placeholder=\"Your Comment\" maxlength=\"65525\" required></textarea></p>\n        <p class=\"form-field comment-form-author\"><input id=\"author\" name=\"author\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Name\" value=\"\" size=\"30\" maxlength=\"245\"></p>\n        <p class=\"form-field comment-form-email\"><input id=\"email\" name=\"email\" type=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" value=\"\" size=\"30\" maxlength=\"100\"></p>\n        <p class=\"comment-form-cookies-consent\"><input id=\"wp-comment-cookies-consent\" name=\"wp-comment-cookies-consent\" type=\"checkbox\" value=\"yes\"> <label for=\"wp-comment-cookies-consent\">Save my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment. </label></p>\n        <p class=\"form-submit\"><input name=\"submit\" type=\"submit\" id=\"comment-submit\" class=\"submit\" value=\"Post Comment\"> <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"comment_post_ID\" value=\"532824\" id=\"comment_post_ID\"> <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"comment_parent\" id=\"comment_parent\" value=\"0\"></p>\n        <input type=\"hidden\" id=\"ct_checkjs_28f0b864598a1291557bed248a998d4e\" name=\"ct_checkjs\" value=\"0\">\n       </form>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "Francesco Romano 的博士论文提出了一种吸气式等离子体推进器，通过收集极低轨道（VLEO）稀薄空气作为推进剂，实验室测试和模型显示其有望实现卫星无限期运行，但尚未经过飞行验证。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "Francesco Romano 的博士论文提出了一种吸气式等离子体推进器，通过收集极低轨道（VLEO）稀薄空气作为推进剂，实验室测试和模型显示其有望实现卫星无限期运行，但尚未经过飞行验证。",
  "summary": "SciTechDaily（改编自 Universe Today）报道了斯图加特大学 Francesco Romano 发表在 arXiv 上的博士论文，该论文提出了一种针对极低地球轨道（约 100-450 公里）卫星的大气呼吸电推进（ABEP）系统。在该轨道高度，大气阻力迫使卫星进行近乎连续的推力维持，并需要携带沉重的 onboard 推进剂。主要障碍包括原子氧对电极、加速栅极和中和器阴极的腐蚀，以及大气固有的变异性。Romano 的设计将优化的进气口——一种涂有石墨或二氧化硅的抛物面镜面反射器，在测试中捕获了约 94.3% 的粒子，且在 15 度倾斜时仅损失 8% 的效率——与非接触式、无中和器的射频螺旋波推进器相结合。该推进器使用类似 MRI 的笼式天线，将 99% 的电功率传输给等离子体，并通过螺线管排出准中性射流，从而无需中和器。真空室测试在 50-60 瓦功率下维持了稳定等离子体；模型表明，在 190 至 250 公里高度之间，使用低于 1.6 千瓦的功率即可实现无限期运行，而在火星上则可在 120-160 公里高度运行。目前尚无飞行演示。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "极低地球轨道对卫星具有吸引力，但使其有价值的大气层同时也导致驻留成本高昂。",
      "explanation": "极低地球轨道（VLEO，约 100-450 公里）能提供更清晰的遥感图像，降低通信和雷达的功耗需求，并使失效卫星自然离轨。但空气阻力会持续减缓航天器速度，因此它们必须几乎连续地提供推力，而传统系统必须携带昂贵的推进剂，如氙气。"
    },
    {
      "point": "原子氧和大气变异性是吸气式发动机的两大主要工程阻碍。",
      "explanation": "紫外线辐射将 O2 分解为原子氧，这会腐蚀金属电极、加速栅极以及用于中和航天器的电子枪阴极；若没有中和作用，带电排气会被吸引回来，导致推力崩溃。此外，大气随昼夜周期、纬度和太阳活动而变化，因此发动机必须在所有条件下保持工作。"
    },
    {
      "point": "Romano 的方案结合了优化进气口与非接触式、无中和器的射频螺旋波等离子体推进器。",
      "explanation": "在三种进气设计中，涂有石墨或二氧化硅的镜面抛物面反射器胜出，它收集了约 94.3% 的粒子，并在 15 度倾斜下仅损失 8% 的效率。受 MRI 启发的笼式天线使 99% 的输入电功率进入推进器，而螺线管产生准中性等离子体射流，消除了被原子氧破坏的中和器的需求。"
    },
    {
      "point": "实验室测试和建模表明，在标准太阳能板功率预算内实现无限期位置保持是可行的。",
      "explanation": "模拟 VLEO 气体浓度的真空室测试仅在 50-60 瓦射频功率下产生了稳定等离子体。应用于耗尽氙气的 GOCE 卫星的模型表明，在 190 至 250 公里之间使用低于 1.6 千瓦的功率可实现无限期运行，而二氧化碳驱动的火星变体可在 120-160 公里高度工作。"
    },
    {
      "point": "该概念仍停留在实验室和仿真结果阶段，并非经过飞行验证的技术。",
